      "title": "Iran school bombing: grounds to believe US was behind atrocity, UN finds",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/17/iran-school-bombing-un-mission-us-military-behind-attack",
      "description": "<p>Fact-finding mission says military strikes on school and sports facility in ⁠February constitute war ⁠crimes</p><p>A UN fact-finding mission has determined there are reasonable grounds to believe the US was behind military strikes on a school and a sports facility in Iran in ⁠February that killed 120 children, and that these constituted war ⁠crimes.</p><p>The school strike, which killed 156 civilians including 120 children, involved a US Tomahawk missile that collapsed the roof of the Shajareh Tayyebeh<sup> </sup>primary school, which the UN said was “clearly identifiable”, in Minab, Hormozgan province, on 28 February.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/17/iran-school-bombing-un-mission-us-military-behind-attack\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-17T13:22:35"
    }
